│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ tail_objective_search                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the biased sorted-coordinate initialization with unbiased uniform sampling in the │
│                          │ reference triangle, and optimize a lower-tail objective rather than only the single       │
│                          │ smallest determinant. The Heilbronn objective is nonsmooth: improving one active triangle │
│                          │ often requires temporarily reducing the current minimum while increasing several nearly   │
│                          │ active constraints. A weighted average of the smallest triangle determinants provides     │
│                          │ this needed guidance while the recorded incumbent is still selected strictly by the true  │
│                          │ minimum area. The reduced temperature is scaled to this more informative local objective  │
│                          │ and avoids excessively random late-stage moves.                                           │
