│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ critical_triangle_guidance                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Bias proposed mutations toward vertices involved in the currently smallest triangles. The │
│                          │ minimum-area objective is controlled by a small active set of constraints; uniformly      │
│                          │ selecting a point wastes most iterations moving points that cannot improve the            │
│                          │ bottleneck. The added helper identifies vertices appearing in the 18 smallest triangles   │
│                          │ and assigns them higher sampling probability, while retaining a nonzero probability for   │
│                          │ every point to avoid premature trapping. This is especially useful during annealing,      │
│                          │ where repair moves should predominantly affect active near-degenerate triples.            │
