│ patch_description        │ This implementation replaces stochastic single-point annealing with deterministic         │
│                          │ alternating linear programming. With all x-coordinates fixed, every signed triangle       │
│                          │ determinant is linear in the y-coordinates; conversely, with y fixed it is linear in x.   │
│                          │ The algorithm preserves the oriented-matroid sign pattern of each seeded arrangement and  │
│                          │ alternately solves exact max-min linear programs for x and y, monotonically improving the │
│                          │ bottleneck triangle area. Multiple deterministic low-discrepancy and jittered lattice     │
│                          │ seeds explore distinct sign patterns efficiently, while every point remains inside the    │
│                          │ fixed unit-area reference triangle.                                                       │
