│ patch_name               │ bottleneck_simplex13                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ This implementation replaces the purely random point set with a deterministic             │
│                          │ bottleneck-optimization search inside a fixed unit-area-equivalent simplex. Three points  │
│                          │ are held at the simplex vertices, guaranteeing a convex hull of known area, while the     │
│                          │ remaining ten points are optimized using a reproducible annealed local search.            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The search uses all 286 triangle areas simultaneously. It combines a soft-min objective   │
│                          │ during exploration, which improves clusters of nearly-degenerate triangles rather than    │
│                          │ only the single worst one, with a final strict minimum-area objective. Candidate moves    │
│                          │ preferentially perturb points occurring in the currently smallest triangles, providing a  │
│                          │ targeted bottleneck-repair mechanism. The returned configuration is deterministic because │
│                          │ all randomness is generated from a fixed seed.                                            │
