│ patch_name               │ fixed_simplex_search                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the variable-hull square search with a fixed reference simplex. Fixing three      │
│                          │ points at the vertices of a triangle removes irrelevant affine and hull-area degrees of   │
│                          │ freedom: every candidate has the same hull, every interior point is feasible by           │
│                          │ construction, and the normalized triangle area is directly its determinant. This also     │
│                          │ eliminates repeated monotone-chain hull computations, allowing the existing annealing     │
│                          │ budget to spend its time on meaningful geometric moves.                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The initialization and mutation operators are changed to sample/project only the ten      │
│                          │ movable points into the reference triangle. Keeping a small margin from the boundary      │
│                          │ prevents accidental duplicate vertex/boundary placements while retaining essentially the  │
│                          │ full feasible region.                                                                     │
