│ patch_description        │ Introduce occasional coupled two-point proposals drawn from the union of several tight    │
│                          │ triangles. The current search almost always changes one vertex of one active constraint,  │
│                          │ which can stall when improving that vertex merely transfers the bottleneck to a           │
│                          │ neighboring near-collinear triple. Coordinated moves permit the search to reorganize a    │
│                          │ small local cluster while retaining the existing lower-tail annealing objective. They use │
│                          │ a reduced per-point step size to avoid destabilizing the configuration and remain         │
│                          │ deterministic under the existing seeded generator.                                        │
