│ patch_description        │ Focus proposals on vertices participating in the current smallest-area triangles, since   │
│                          │ these near-collinear triples are the active constraints limiting the maximin objective.   │
│                          │ In addition to the existing occasional global shake, introduce deterministic-probability  │
│                          │ coordinated two-point moves from the union of vertices in the eight worst triangles. Such │
│                          │ moves are important because a single bottleneck vertex often cannot move alone without    │
│                          │ immediately making another triple limiting. The proposal remains annealed and fully       │
│                          │ reproducible through the existing seeded generator.                                       │
