│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ adaptive_restart_refinement                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Replace equal-budget independent anneals with an adaptive two-stage allocation. First,    │
│                          │ run a broad set of inexpensive structured searches to identify promising orientation/sign │
│                          │ patterns. Then retain only the strongest states and spend the remaining budget on         │
│                          │ substantially longer reheated refinements. This preserves deterministic behavior and      │
│                          │ approximately the existing evaluation budget, while concentrating expensive optimization  │
│                          │ on configurations that have already demonstrated a strong lower-tail triangle-area        │
│                          │ distribution. The refinement starts at a lower perturbation scale than a fresh anneal so  │
│                          │ it improves active bottlenecks rather than repeatedly destroying a good hull/interior     │
│                          │ arrangement.                                                                              │
