│                          │ the best configuration found during the initial global-search phase. The Heilbronn        │
│                          │ objective has many sign-pattern and active-triangle basins; random starts are useful for  │
│                          │ discovering promising basins, while additional search budget is usually more valuable     │
│                          │ when spent refining an already strong arrangement. Continuations use a smaller initial    │
│                          │ displacement and lower temperature than exploratory runs, preserving the established      │
│                          │ geometric structure while allowing active constraints to change and escape shallow local  │
│                          │ maxima. The total annealing iteration budget remains 84,000, so runtime should remain     │
│                          │ comparable.                                                                               │
