│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ ring_active13                                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ This implementation replaces the fixed triangular-hull search with a rotationally         │
│                          │ structured polygonal hull and an active-constraint annealing strategy. It keeps a regular │
│                          │ outer ring fixed, which makes the convex hull area constant and removes expensive dynamic │
│                          │ hull calculations, while allowing the remaining points to occupy a substantially less     │
│                          │ restrictive region than a reference triangle.                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The search uses several deterministic hull layouts (primarily 7- and 8-sided outer        │
│                          │ rings), structured ring initializations, lower-tail scoring over the smallest triangle    │
│                          │ determinants, active-triple-guided mutations, annealed acceptance, and a final coordinate │
│                          │ polishing stage. Interior points are projected into the incircle of the fixed polygon,    │
│                          │ guaranteeing that the outer ring remains the convex hull throughout optimization.         │
