│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ guided_symmetric_search                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Introduce two geometry-aware improvements without changing the fixed convex reference     │
│                          │ region or the deterministic search model.                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ First, add a signed-area gradient for a chosen point in a bottleneck triangle. Random     │
│                          │ isotropic moves spend most proposals changing triangle area inefficiently; moving a       │
│                          │ selected vertex along the normal to its opposite edge directly increases that triangle’s  │
│                          │ determinant. The proposal retains a random component, preserving the ability to resolve   │
│                          │ competing active constraints.                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Second, use affine threefold-symmetric barycentric initializations on half of the         │
│                          │ restarts. The reference triangle admits the cyclic barycentric map `(x,y) -> (1-x-y,x)`,  │
│                          │ so a center point plus three three-point orbits gives exactly the ten non-corner points   │
│                          │ required. Such starts provide a much more balanced global distribution than purely random │
│                          │ samples while subsequent unconstrained local moves can break symmetry if beneficial.      │
│ num_applied              │ 3                                                                                         │
