│ patch_description        │ The current program fixes a three-vertex triangular hull, uses 8 restarts × 18,000        │
│                          │ iterations, a 16-triangle lower-tail surrogate, Gaussian moves with initial scale 0.100,  │
│                          │ 18% paired moves, and temperature `0.0017*(1-progress)^2+8e-6`. Its triangular-hull       │
│                          │ restriction prevents exploration of the empirically stronger circular nine-point hull     │
│                          │ structure.                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new algorithm uses a fixed regular nine-point convex hull and optimizes four interior │
│                          │ points. This preserves feasibility without repeated hull projection while directly        │
│                          │ exploiting the recommended circular-hull prior. The search uses 14 deterministic          │
│                          │ complementary starts, 7,500 annealing iterations per start, a tighter active set that     │
│                          │ decreases from 24 to 8 constraints, directed gradients for bottleneck triangles,          │
│                          │ occasional coordinated two-point moves, and a final strict greedy refinement. The hull is │
│                          │ fixed, so normalized area is computed efficiently as determinant divided by the nonagon's │
│                          │ twice-area.                                                                               │
