│ patch_name               │ fix_nine_hull_polish                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The search explicitly uses a nine-vertex fixed hull, but the polishing pass incorrectly   │
│                          │ clamps the inferred hull size to 8. This makes the ninth true boundary point movable      │
│                          │ during polishing and normalizes its determinant score using an octagonal hull area.       │
│                          │ Consequently, the final polish can optimize an inconsistent objective and may even return │
│                          │ a configuration whose hull is no longer the intended fixed nonagon.                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Allowing the inferred count to remain 9 restores consistent feasibility, preserves all    │
│                          │ nine boundary vertices, and uses the correct nonagon hull area and incircle radius. This  │
│                          │ is a zero-cost correctness improvement to the most refined stage of the optimization.     │
