│ patch_name               │ active_set_sampling                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ Replace repeated selection of the single currently worst triangle with probabilistic      │
│                          │ sampling from a low-area active set. Maximin optima are governed by several nearly tight  │
│                          │ triangle constraints; always moving only the unique worst triangle tends to oscillate     │
│                          │ between a few constraints. Sampling low-area triangles with inverse-area weights retains  │
│                          │ strong pressure on bottlenecks while allowing the search to resolve competing active      │
│                          │ constraints. The discovery stage uses a narrow active set and the longer refinement stage │
│                          │ uses a broader one.                                                                       │
