│ patch_name               │ active_gradient_simplex13                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ This implementation switches from a fixed many-vertex polygon hull to an                  │
│                          │ affine-normalized reference triangle, which makes every determinant directly equal to     │
│                          │ triangle area divided by hull area. The search uses a deterministic active-constraint     │
│                          │ gradient ensemble: it identifies the lower-tail triangles, accumulates their signed       │
│                          │ determinant gradients at participating movable points, and proposes batched moves         │
│                          │ combining these directions with annealed noise. This is followed by strict minimum-area   │
│                          │ coordinate polishing using active triangle normals and stencil directions.                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The approach retains the useful lower-tail idea from prior programs, but replaces random  │
│                          │ active-point perturbation as the primary engine with a constraint-driven subgradient      │
│                          │ method. The fixed triangular hull also eliminates hull-area bookkeeping and guarantees    │
│                          │ feasibility through simplex projection.                                                   │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
