│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ active_constraint_polish                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Add a deterministic strict-score polishing phase after the existing tail-aware pattern    │
│                          │ search. The current final search can accept equal-minimum moves based on lower-tail       │
│                          │ energy, which is useful for basin discovery but may stop short of improving the primary   │
│                          │ normalized minimum-area metric. This pass considers only strict primary-score             │
│                          │ improvements.                                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Directions are generated from the currently smallest triangles: for each active vertex,   │
│                          │ use normals to its opposite active edges, supplemented by radial and tangential           │
│                          │ directions around the point centroid. These are geometrically meaningful directions for   │
│                          │ increasing the altitude, and therefore area, of bottleneck triangles. A shrinking stencil │
│                          │ provides a reproducible active-set refinement without materially changing the             │
│                          │ global-search cost.                                                                       │
